This file exists only to keep Content/Maps/ in Git — Git tracks files, not
directories, and an empty directory would vanish on clone.

WHAT IS ACTUALLY COMMITTED HERE (checked with `git ls-files Content/Maps`, and
this paragraph replaces a note that said the opposite):

  Arena.umap         COMMITTED. Deliberately EMPTY — the whole arena (floor,
                     walls, cover, endzones, lights, player starts, skyline) is
                     built in C++ by ATraceArenaBuilder at BeginPlay, so the
                     asset carries no content. Scripts/generate-map.sh recreates
                     it from scratch if it is ever lost, which is why the old
                     note called it "generated on demand" — but it is in the
                     repo, and a clone does not have to run anything.
  Arena_Baked.umap   COMMITTED — the SHIPPING map, and the only one with real
                     content. It is Arena run once and written down: ~590
                     editable actors, One File Per Actor, so the .umap itself is
                     a few KB and the actors live in
                     Content/__ExternalActors__/Maps/Arena_Baked/ (~600 packages,
                     also committed).
  MainMenu.umap      COMMITTED.
  Fish_*.umap        COMMITTED — a collaborator's test maps. Kept, not touched.

HOW Arena_Baked IS REGENERATED, and the rule that governs it:

  /Game/Maps/Arena is the source of truth for every PROCEDURAL family. Builder
  changes are never hand-copied into Arena_Baked; they arrive via a re-bake.
  Arena_Baked is also the only home of the HAND layer (the centre kit and its
  dress strips, hand-placed lamps, hand-moved pieces).

  Scripts/bake-arena.sh --force            destroys the hand layer. Use it only
                                           on a level nobody has edited.
  Scripts/rebake-arena-preserving.py       the one to use: census -> force bake
                                           -> replay deletions and hand
                                           transforms -> restore the hand layer
                                           -> reconciliation. See MAP plan §10.

.umap and .uasset go through Git LFS and are `lockable` (see .gitattributes),
which means git-lfs checks them out read-only until somebody takes a lock —
lock before you edit, and note that the bake scripts clear the read-only bit on
exactly the two things they rewrite:

    git lfs lock Content/Maps/Arena_Baked.umap
